# Normalize text files to LF in the repository and on checkout. core.autocrlf
# is unset/false here, so nothing was normalizing line endings on its own —
# different editors and tools writing to the same files (CRLF from Windows
# editors, LF from other tooling) had been accumulating as mixed endings
# inside individual committed files, which turns even small logical diffs
# into noisy whole-file diffs. This only affects files as they're next
# written through git (add/commit); it does not retroactively touch content
# already in history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary types: never attempt text conversion on these regardless of
# git's own content-sniffing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.riv binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
